uses g++ to compile
python: 3.13

For Python,
```
    python conway.py --arg
    --save      | Save to default file, output.txt
    --graphics  | Use graphics in terminal
    --output    | specify output file and saves it
    --input     | Use a starter input file
    --gen       | Specify generations to run, default 10
```
Files are set up as:

8 8  -> Width Height
0    -> Generations that have passed
5    -> Living Cells
[1, 2], [2, 3], [3, 3], [3, 2], [3, 1] -> Coordinates of each cell
